WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.960 --> 00:00:10.530
The hundredth anniversary of the Sykes-Picot
Agreement has highlighted the artificiality

00:00:10.530 --> 00:00:13.420
of many of the borders of countries in the
Middle East.

00:00:13.420 --> 00:00:17.590
Now some people talk about, with the rise
of the Islamic State, that maybe it's time

00:00:17.590 --> 00:00:18.940
to draw new borders.

00:00:18.940 --> 00:00:24.029
Well, that's essentially imperialism 2.0,
but even if someone were to do it, would it

00:00:24.029 --> 00:00:25.939
really resolve any of the conflicts?

00:00:25.939 --> 00:00:28.779
The people in the Middle East don't live in
neat little pockets.

00:00:28.779 --> 00:00:33.399
They're all spread about, and so there's no
way to draw the border that simply includes

00:00:33.399 --> 00:00:36.690
one group on one side, and the other group
on the other side.

00:00:36.690 --> 00:00:41.210
Any resulting state is going to have a minority,
and therefore a potential for conflict.

00:00:41.210 --> 00:00:45.040
If we were simply to redraw borders, what
would the second, third, fourth, fifth and

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:46.649
sixth order effects be?

00:00:46.649 --> 00:00:49.130
Consider for example the partition of India.

00:00:49.130 --> 00:00:50.649
That was supposed to resolve conflict

00:00:50.649 --> 00:00:55.589
but if you look at all the displaced people
that came from the partition in 1947

00:00:55.589 --> 00:00:59.610
and impose the same definition of refugee
that's used for the Palestinians, there's

00:00:59.610 --> 00:01:03.309
over 200 million refugees in South Asia

00:01:03.309 --> 00:01:07.950
and the resulting states point nuclear weapons
at each other.

00:01:07.950 --> 00:01:13.560
People criticize the borders as being an imperial
legacy, but to redraw the borders—wouldn’t

00:01:13.560 --> 00:01:16.500
that just be Imperialism version 2.0?

00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:20.390
Let us know your thoughts in the comments
and any other questions you’d like us to

00:01:20.390 --> 00:01:21.479
answer in 60 seconds.

